# Build output — `kernel/`, `xtask/`, and the root workspace each produce
# their own `target/` (see CLAUDE.md's "Workspace layout" on why they're
# separate builds); xtask also writes bootable images to the root
# `target/` (see xtask/src/main.rs's `image_from_binary`). `Cargo.lock` in
# all three is intentionally *not* ignored here — this workspace produces
# binaries/bootable images, not a library, so lockfiles are committed for
# reproducible builds, not left to `cargo`'s default per-crate judgment.
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.bak
*.pdb

# Bootable disk images, in case one is ever built outside `target/`.
*.img

# QEMU/manual debugging output — serial capture logs from ad hoc local runs
# (the checked-in `kernel/tests/*.rs` are the real, reproducible tests).
*.log

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS-generated junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local environment overrides — never commit secrets/machine-specific config.
.env
.env.local

# Claude Code tooling and its generated docs — local development aid only,
# kept out of the public GitHub repo on purpose (not a build artifact, so
# it's called out separately from everything above).
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
docs/THREAT_MODEL.md
